WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you've been
doing comedy your whole life.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of improv stuff,
sketch stuff.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, sure.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.606 size:81% position:41%
-I did not know that
you dabbled in standup

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:07.307 size:75% position:38% line:92%
in your early years.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I had --
Standup is interesting for me,

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.912
because I've actually -- I did
a lot of it when I was younger,

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:20.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I hit a wall
called two kids.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:23.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
And most standup shows
don't start till, you know,

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
at least 8:00 p.m.,
and, usually,

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.192 line:92%
you're on at 10:00 or 11:00.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:31.831
And one night doing standup in
L.A., I fell asleep at the mic.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was at the mic
and I did that thing you do

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.869 line:92%
when you're driving at 3:00 a.m.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.638 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I just went...

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:42.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
In the middle of my jokes.
And I said, "That's it.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:46.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't be falling --
You can't sleep."

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.680 line:92%
I had one goal as a standup.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.684
I always thought, "You know, if
I can just entertain one person

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:58.058
and if that person can be me,
I'll feel good about this."

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But then, yeah,
that's out the window

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.561 line:92%
if you put yourself to sleep.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.162 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.531
-Then you weren't even
succeeding on that level.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, no.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:09.803
-We talked before on this show
about how important a show to me

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:11.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Mr. Show" was
that you did with David Cross.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Does anyone know it?

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was this
obscure, little show.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a wonderful show.
-Well, you can still see it.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:18.711
-And then I believe it
holds up incredibly well.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:19.245 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Every time I think of
a "Mr. Show" sketch

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
and go watch it on YouTube,
I'm always thinking,

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Man, this is just as good
as it ever was."

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:26.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you doing stuff
before that?

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:27.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you and David
doing stuff before that

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
that made sense as to
what that show ended up being?

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:32.625 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I was.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.662
I started in radio,
at Southern Illinois University.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:39.499
And I had a show called
"The Prime Time Special."

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was on Thursday nights
at midnight.

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:44.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it was not
in prime time or special.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:49.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was kind of "Mr. Show."
We had a thematic story.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
My partner was
Tim Thomas, very funny,

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:55.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
very much like David,
in a lot of ways.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
And David had "Cross Comedy,"
which was in

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:01.688
Boston and New York, that was
also exactly like "Mr. Show."

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:02.956 line:92%
So we were really heading

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
towards that
wonderful connection.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is such a good
show, and I highly recommend,

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
for those who haven't seen it,
to go back and watch it,

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:11.764
'cause, like I said, it is
as good now as it ever was.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm so happy
"Better Call Saul" is back.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.535 size:84% position:42%
It's such a great show.
-Thanks. Monday night.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:16.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
All right.
-Monday night, everybody.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.672
-Thank you.
-Fourth season, August 6th, AMC.

